A||||7||Sootah||How hard is it to add a 3rd brake light to an '85?||||1||
Z||000000||Sootah||12-28-2001||06:17 PM||||My car may be back on the road soon (don't know exactly when, details still tenative) and I'd like to add the 3rd brake light to my car. How hard is this? (Wireing, etc)<P>Also, Chester, what kinda brake light is it that you have? I really like that.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__tig_sig2.gif">           <BR><sup><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Black_Beauty_-_Front_Right.jpg" TARGET=_blank>The Black Beauty</A> (85 GT) - <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Busted-Ass_SE.jpg" TARGET=_blank>Bustedato</A> (86 SE, Parts car)<BR><I>Don't sweat the petty things, and don't pet the sweaty things</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AOL IM</B>: KSSouter<BR><B>MSN IM</B>: I_R_Sootah@hotmail.com<BR></sup>||||reg||1
Z||000001||snafus87||12-28-2001||06:50 PM||||I'm not really sure how hard it would be for the notchback style, because the brakes ARE the turn signals...but in the fastbacks (as my 85 is) its just a splice and go deal...find the wire that's hot when you hit the brakes and tap in and you should be set...I think you might be able to get a relay or something to bypass the turn signals, but you'd be better off waiting for someone with a little more electircal expertise to reply...I know these guys are out there..<P>------------------<BR>JT Krupa<BR>85 GT<BR>(fastback conversion)<BR>180+ K miles<BR>Lehighton, PA||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||12-28-2001||07:00 PM||||Easiest way is to run an additional wire right from the brake pedal switch to the 3rd light.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-28-2001||07:05 PM||||yea, or it will blink with turn signals. I had to totally rewire all the lights to get my kits lites to work rite. red tail lite/w red stop lites inboard. amber to work only on turn sigs outboard. DO yours by running a new wire from brake pedal switch to the window brake lite. If you have cruise make sure you connect to the right switch, one is to disengage the cruise control.<P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/rogergarrison1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sootah||12-28-2001||11:05 PM||||Cool, thanx guys. Anybody here know what taillight chester has?||||reg||2
Z||000005||88CoupeV6||12-28-2001||11:22 PM||||I thought chester had his stock tail & 3rd brake lights. Got a pic of his car so I can see what you are referring to on it?<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||5
Z||000006||gargoyle||12-29-2001||03:26 PM||||I have a question that is sort of related to this topic. Is it legal to remove the third brake light. I have an 87 GT and I'm thinking about removing it. I never did like those things. Just curious.||||reg||5
Z||000007||theogre||12-29-2001||03:58 PM||||Leagally, Federally, it's required for all cars 86 and newer. If you have inspections, you may not pass w/o it. Don't know what your state does....<P>The light may not look the best but it's probably saved you getting rear ended more often than you think. When you are being tail gated by large vehicles the high mount lamp may be all they see it you tap the brakes.... ||||reg||1
